  "site_name": "Canada Water Masterplan - Land Bounded By Lower Road (West), Redriff Road (South), Quebec Way (East)\rSurrey Quays Road And Canada Water Dock (North)\rAnd Site At Roberts Close\rLondon SE16\r\r\r",
  "description": "Non material amendment submitted under s96a of the TCPA 1990 (As amended) for planning application 18/AP/1604 dated 29/05/2020 which granted Hybrid Planning Permission for the comprehensive redevelopment of the Canada Water Masterplan comprising Outline planning permission (all matters reserved) for the demolition of all existing structures and redevelopment to include a number of tall buildings comprising the following mix of uses: retail (Use Classes A1-A5), workspace (B1), hotel (C1), residential (C3), assisted living (C2), student accommodation, leisure (including a cinema) (D2), community facilities (including health and education uses) (D1), public toilets, nightclub, flexible events space, an energy centre, an interim and permanent petrol filling station, a primary electricity substation, a secondary entrance for Surrey Quays Rail Station, a Park Pavilion, landscaping including open spaces and public realm, works to the Canada Water Dock, car parking, means of access, associated infrastructure and highways works and demolition or retention with alterations to the Press Hall and/or the Spine Building of the Printworks; and Detailed planning permission for the Development Plots in Phase 1.\r\rThis application seeks to amend the Description of Development to remove references to Use Classes in relation to the outline proposals. The Description of Development specifies the land uses applied for and the associated Use Classes are defined in the Development Specification and Condition 5 of the Planning Permission. Any changes to Condition 5 would need to be secured through a separate planning application.\r\r",
